# L §4.5 (tally 2.1.8 R12, #169-f; T's fixes/g6b/b3_q): a removal known in a window that holds the cut removes the row
# or not, so the restatement before it stands with its legs that hole, naming the row and the removal's version (q);
# windows each 0.00, then 12.00 (q2). 2.1.7's refcore skipped the row: 0.00 PLN.
=== m.tally
model p
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-01
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-10, kind: transfers, leg cash from world to konto amount 12.00 PLN) "r1"

version fx
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-20)
  replace bank[r1] = none "r1"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) as known 2026-04-10
ask q2: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) as known 2026-04-10 windows each
ask q3: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) as known 2026-04-21
ask q4: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) as known 2026-04-04
=== expect
q: ?"date within window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-20) not precise enough for the cut 2026-04-10" (bank[r1], fx)
  cut 2026-04-10
q2 [known of fx = 2026-04-05 .. 2026-04-10]: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2026-04-10
q2 [known of fx = 2026-04-11 .. 2026-04-20]: 12.00 PLN
  cut 2026-04-10
q3: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2026-04-21
q4: 12.00 PLN
  cut 2026-04-04
